    what: 'Action research in which villagers themselves used the Right to Information Act to pursue entitlements they had been denied, with the research following what happened when they did. Three villages were adopted as Action Research Villages for a year — Taj Khodai in Chittaura block, and Nai Basti and Nishad Nagar in Mihinpurwa — and 588 applications were filed from them on the Public Distribution System, land entitlement, roads, drainage, irrigation, forest issues, flood rehabilitation and social security.',
